//// large-object-literals-run-once.js
// Object literals with more properties than fit the short forms, with names that look like indices, and with a name written twice: at the top level of a module, in a function that
// the top level calls once, in a function called often and in a loop. The keys come in the order the language says, each evaluation makes a new object, the last of two equal names wins.
